## Research Complete

I conducted a comprehensive search across 7 different research angles (full AI IDEs, CLIs/terminal agents, workflow-specific tools, project-long memory agents, open-source agents, IDE-integrated tools, and workflow orchestration agents) looking for AI coding tools launched in the last 14 days (June 28 - July 12, 2026).

### Key Finding:

After filtering by launch date (within 14 days of July 12, 2026) and relevance to AI coding/developer workflows, I found **one valid product**:

**Termi Protocol** - Launched July 3, 2026
- A 3D visualization platform for AI coding agents that lets developers watch their CLI agents (Claude Code, Codex, Gemini, etc.) work as robots in an immersive 3D workspace
- Features include multi-agent sync mode, file locks, checkpoints for time-travel debugging, on-device memory, and one-tap approval for risky actions
- Achieved #5 on Product Hunt with 186 upvotes
- Local-first architecture with no backend required for visualization

The result has been written to `new-product.json` in the required JSON format.

### Sources:
- Product Hunt leaderboard and product pages
- GitHub trending repositories
- AI coding tool directories and blogs

**Note:** While I found mentions of other tools like **Aura** (semantic version control for AI agents), those were launched earlier (May 2026 based on "2mo ago" timestamp) and thus fell outside the 14-day window.

